<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Akwamu</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1730 CE (approx.) · capital Nyanaoase</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Akan kingdom that dominated the eastern Gold Coast in the late 17th century, conquering the Ga and seizing a Danish castle.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Akwamu was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> migrants in the hills north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a>, with its capital at Nyanaoase. By the mid-17th century it controlled trade routes from the forest to the coast, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ansa-sasraku">Ansa Sasraku</a> it conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ga-kingdom">Ga kingdom</a> between 1677 and 1681, gaining access to the European forts at Accra.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Akwamu's kings ruled a military empire stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volta-river">Volta</a> and beyond, extracting tribute and slaves from conquered peoples. In 1693 an Akwamu trader, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asameni">Asameni</a>, seized the Danish castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osu-castle">Christiansborg</a> and held it for a year. Akonno, king in the early 18th century, extended Akwamu power east across the Volta.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1730 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/akyem-abuakwa">Akyem Abuakwa</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-akyem-kotoku">Akyem Kotoku</a> and the Ga defeated Akwamu, which moved east across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volta-river">Volta</a> to Akwamufie. It survived there as a smaller state under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> and later the British.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1600 CE – 1730 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:2.59%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1730 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nyanaoase</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ansa Sasraku, Akonno</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Akan religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Twi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Ghana, Togo</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Akwamu Empire, Kingdom of Akwamu</dd></dl></aside></div>

